  "articleBody": "Taking out an interior partition seems straightforward until you realize that hidden structure carries ceiling joists or a second floor. Hiring the right framing contractor for your remodel protects the integrity of your home and keeps your project moving smoothly.\n\nWhat to Expect During the Process:\n- Initial Evaluation: A qualified contractor confirms whether a wall carries structural weight, checks how loads transfer downward, and reviews if engineered lumber or temporary shoring is required.\n- Building Department Approvals: Remodels that modify load-bearing assemblies, shear walls, or fire separations require proper building permits and structural details before demolition begins.\n- Coordinated Rough Work: Once structural members, headers, and fire blocking are installed, rough plumbing, electrical, and HVAC work must be completed before framing inspections happen.\n\nNever allow walls to be enclosed before rough inspections pass. Concealing framing behind drywall without sign-offs can halt construction and force expensive tear-outs. If your remodel involves multi-story load paths, roof alteration, or engineered beams, having hands-on structural leadership is essential.\n\nReady to open up your living space? Contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your remodel framing plans.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}